cerberus (0.10.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New cerberus-vsock-watch package: a detective control for SIGN-1
    (docs/THREAT-MODEL.md) — alerts on any AF_VSOCK connect() to the enclave
    from a process other than cerberus-api, via two independent detectors
    (an auditd rule and an eBPF tracepoint probe). Does not close the
    underlying gap; makes exploitation observable. See
    docs/vsock-connect-detection.md.

 -- Paul Kilar <pkilar@gmail.com>  Wed, 22 Jul 2026 09:50:00 -0400

cerberus (0.9.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * LDAP backends can now discover servers via DNS SRV records (srv: block with
    tls_mode) and fail over across them per RFC 2782, in addition to a fixed
    url:.

 -- Paul Kilar <pkilar@gmail.com>  Fri, 10 Jul 2026 20:50:19 -0400

cerberus (0.8.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian packaging, mirroring the RPM and Arch packaging. Multi-binary
    source package producing:
    - cerberus-api: the host-side HTTPS gateway service.
    - cerberus-signer: the Nitro Enclave signer service (binary, wrapper, unit).
    - cerberus-client: the cssh shell wrapper (Architecture: all).
    - cerberus-signer-eif: opt-in, built only under the pkg.cerberus.eif build
      profile; bundles a prebuilt EIF carrying per-deployment CA key material.
  * Service env files live in /etc/default/; the cerberus user and
    /var/log/cerberus are created via sysusers.d/tmpfiles.d; units are installed
    without being enabled or started (they need site config and a Nitro host).

 -- Paul Kilar <pkilar@gmail.com>  Thu, 09 Jul 2026 18:00:00 -0400
